.TH ISA-TOP 1
.SH NAME
isa-top \- display statistics of captured packets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B isa-top
.B -i interface
[\f -s \fRb|p]
[\f -t\fR num]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B isa-top
captures packets, calculates b/s and p/s, sorts by bytes/packets/s depending on the argument provided, and then displays the statistics. It always shows the top 10 most communicating packets.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i
Sets the interface for packet capture.
.TP
.BR \-s
Sets the output sorting by bytes/packets/s. Default value is b.
.TP
.BR \-t
Sets the time interval for displaying statistics. Default value is 1.
